<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oda Nobunaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1534">1534</a>–<a href="/years/1582">1582</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oda Nobunaga was a Japanese warlord of the sixteenth century who began the military unification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> served as his ally. After Nobunaga's death in 1582, his work was continued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> and completed by Ieyasu, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga.jpg" alt="Oda Nobunaga" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 狩野宗秀 (Kanō Sōshū, 1551 - 1601) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Odanobunaga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
